# Commit and Deployment Default

## Commit first, always
- Automatically commit after any completed code change. Do not wait to be asked.
- Order is always: commit, then push to `origin/main`, then deploy.
- Never end a task with uncommitted code changes. Vercel CLI deploys upload the
  working directory, so a green production deploy does NOT mean the work is in
  git. Verify with `git status` before finishing.
- Write a real commit message describing why the change was made. On Windows
  PowerShell, heredoc (`<<'EOF'`) does not work — write the message to a temp
  file and use `git commit -F <file>`.
- Do not commit files that likely contain secrets. Flag them instead.
- Do not commit large binaries (video, large media). `public/*.mp4` is gitignored.

## Then deploy
- Never leave code changes undeployed at the end of a task unless the user
  explicitly says not to deploy.
- After deployment, always return both:
  - production/live URL
  - Vercel inspect URL
- If deployment fails, retry immediately and report the blocker plus what was attempted.
